\section{Hit calling}{

A significant overall test alone can arise without any concentration
differing from the vehicle control, so a hit needs both:
\itemize{
\item ANOVA: overall \code{p_value < alpha} and at least one Dunnett
p-value \verb{< alpha}.
\item Repeated-measures ANOVA: first the full model, concentration x
phase \code{p < alpha} and at least one within-phase Dunnett p-value
\verb{< alpha} (hit "via interaction"); otherwise the reduced model,
concentration \code{p < alpha} and at least one Dunnett p-value \verb{< alpha}
(hit "via reduced").
}
A missing p-value that would decide the outcome gives \code{"indeterminate"}
instead of a hit or non-hit. \code{hit_p_value} is the p-value of the overall
test that gave the hit, and \code{neg_log10_p_hit} its \code{-log10}.
}

